+tresc_en: |
+  ## Four patrons
+
+  The site is built around four mathematicians who, after the war, built mathematics in Wrocław from the ground up. Each of them is the patron of one section of the site and gives it its colour, and the Institute's lecture rooms bear their names.
+
+  - **Institute** — Edward Marczewski (1907–1976) · amber · room EM
+  - **Research** — Władysław Ślebodziński (1884–1972) · emerald · room WS
+  - **Study** — Bronisław Knaster (1893–1980) · azure · room B
+  - **Outreach** — Hugo Steinhaus (1887–1972) · raspberry · room HS
+
+  The patron's face is drawn line by line when you enter the section page, and the page headers show facts from his life and mathematics, drawn at random for each visit.
+
+  ## Image sources
+
+  - **Sketches of the patrons**, based on photographs: Władysław Ślebodziński (1938) and Hugo Steinhaus (1968) — Wikimedia Commons ([Ślebodziński](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:W%C5%82adys%C5%82aw_%C5%9Alebodzi%C5%84ski.jpg), [Steinhaus](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hugo_Steinhaus.jpg)), public domain; Edward Marczewski and Bronisław Knaster — MacTutor History of Mathematics, University of St Andrews ([Marczewski](https://mathshistory.st-andrews.ac.uk/Biographies/Marczewski/), [Knaster](https://mathshistory.st-andrews.ac.uk/Biographies/Knaster/pictdisplay/)).
+  - **Signatures**, from reproductions: Edward Marczewski — *Nowa Księga Szkocka* (New Scottish Book), vol. I, entry of 7 July 1946 ([Library of the Faculty of Mathematics and Computer Science, University of Wrocław](https://wmi.uwr.edu.pl/biblioteka-wydzialowa/nowa-ksiega-szkocka/)); Władysław Ślebodziński — membership card of 1948, in: H. Langner-Matuszczyk, *Władysław Ślebodziński – matematyk, więzień KL Auschwitz nr 79053*, „Śląska Republika Uczonych”, vol. 7, 2016 ([publication page](https://sites.google.com/pwr.edu.pl/slebodzinski/strona-g%C5%82%C3%B3wna)); Bronisław Knaster (1946) and Hugo Steinhaus (1957) — J. Dutkiewicz, *Mieczysław Warmus. Życie i praca naukowa*, 2003 ([Digital Library of the Warsaw University of Technology](https://bcpw.bg.pw.edu.pl/dlibra/publication/1567/edition/1591?language=pl)).
+  - **Campus photograph** on the home page: Corvus monedula, [fotopolska.eu](https://fotopolska.eu/1158570), licence [CC BY-SA 3.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/deed.en); cropped and sharpened.
+
+  ## Found an error?
+
+  At the bottom of every page there is a link “Report an error on this page”. You can also write to the editors: **(address to be added)**.
+
+  ## How this site was made
+
+  Design and development: Szymon Cygan. The content is maintained by the editors in Pages CMS, and the site rebuilds itself a few minutes after every change. The code is open: [IM-UWr/Web-Core on GitHub](https://github.com/IM-UWr/Web-Core).
+
+  Typefaces: Brygada 1918 and Manrope (SIL Open Font License); mathematical formulas: KaTeX. The site does not use tracking cookies — details in the [Privacy policy](/polityka-prywatnosci).
+
+  ## Previous website
+
+  A copy of the Institute's previous website is available in the [archive](https://www.math.uni.wroc.pl/).
+opublikowany: true
